+{
+  "verdict": "failed",
+  "checks": [
+    {
+      "id": "A05.1",
+      "result": "fails",
+      "evidence": "agent/src/server.ts:32, agent/src/server.ts:33, agent/src/server.ts:36, agent/src/config.ts:47",
+      "quote": "if (typeId !== manifest.agentTypeId) {\n  app.log.error({ expected: manifest.agentTypeId, actual: typeId }, \"agent type id does not match release manifest\");\nsetAgentTypeId(typeId);\nexport const manifest = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"release/manifest.json\"), \"utf8\"));",
+      "note": "The audit schema requires both identity fields, but a manifest mismatch only logs and increments a metric before the computed type ID is accepted. The only manifest loader reads a fixed release file; inspection of identity, startup, release, deployment, and infrastructure files found no store registering the mismatching ID. Thus records can carry an ID that does not resolve to a stored manifest. The random process instance UUID also has no explicit pod mapping in the supplied configuration."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "A05.2",
+      "result": "unclear",
+      "evidence": "agent/src/config.ts:64, agent/infra/terraform/iam.tf:69",
+      "quote": "  operationalOwner: \"team:agent-platform\",\n        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }",
+      "note": "The agent maps to the platform team and an externally managed SSO on-call group. CODEOWNERS and README add team and channel names, but the repository does not establish the group's current operator or rotation. External SSO/rotation configuration would be needed to decide this check."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "A05.3",
+      "result": "holds",
+      "evidence": "agent/infra/terraform/iam.tf:4, agent/infra/terraform/iam.tf:15, agent/infra/terraform/iam.tf:16, agent/infra/terraform/iam.tf:2",
+      "quote": "  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.",
+      "note": "The runtime principal is dedicated to the clinic agent's HTTP and reminder workloads, which use the same type-ID computation and deployment inputs. Revoking this principal contains that agent type independently of launching-user credentials. The stop flags support global and tenant scope rather than instance targeting, but the check allows type containment as an alternative."
+    }
+  ],
+  "violates": ["Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance."],
+  "note": "A05 fails because startup accepts and audits a computed agent type ID even when it does not match the stored deployment manifest."
